WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.520
It is very quiet today.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.730
Because it's raining.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>I'm looking at two,
maybe three kilometers by foot.</i>

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.530
<i>I'll make it as long as
I don't run into those things...</i>

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.040
How long will your batteries last?

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.750
In my current operational mode,
I can continue for approximately four more days.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.170
So you'll be able to return without any problems?

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.260
Yes. I am able to navigate my way back

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.340
from any site within a three kilometer radius.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.430
Good. Let's go.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.180
Understood.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.560
Hey!

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.030
Please watch your step. There is a bump here.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.200
May I direct your attention here, Mr. Customer?

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.920
The vanilla cream puffs sold
at this store are so popular

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.960
that the queue always
extends well outside the door.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.010
Do you like cream puffs, Mr. Customer?

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.590
Wouldn't know. Haven't exactly had one before.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.850
Anyway, I don't need you to be a tour guide,
I need you to pick up the pace.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.020
I'm in a hurry.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.100
Yes, understood.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.280
Mr. Customer, located on
the fifth floor of this building

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.900
is a beer-hall affiliated with our department store.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.950
Its menu offers fresh seafood and
many different kinds of craft beers.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.830
I'm begging you, cut the chatter
and put that effort into walking faster.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.660
Yes, understood.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.460
Um, Mr. Customer...

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.050
What, need another break?

00:01:55.050 --> 00:02:01.300
Yes. My femoral power unit
has overheated and requires cooling.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.140
How many times have we taken a break?

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.020
This is the fourth stop.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.860
How much distance have we covered?

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.900
Measuring from the entrance of
the Flowercrest Department Store,

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.570
we have travelled 1112 meters.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.580
One kilometer per hour, on average...

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.000
This rain really isn't letting up at all.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.510
Tell me about it.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.130
Mr. Customer, do you like rain?

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.590
No, quite the opposite.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:42.850
I see.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:48.020
To tell you the truth, I love rain.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.440
Because it brings customers into the planetarium?

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.480
Yes, that is correct!

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.900
That's what I thought.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.690
Indeed.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:04.330
Mr. Manager once taught me that
when it rains, the stars feel more precious.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.790
I see.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.290
By the way, Mr. Customer,
what is your line of work?

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.460
I'm a Junker.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.840
Could you elaborate?

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:21.550
In layman's terms...
I'm a garbage collector, I guess.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.100
Garbage collection?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.140
That is a very noble profession.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.690
My body is designed to be completely recyclable...

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:32.730
About time we got going.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.400
You good to go?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.730
Yes, let us continue.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.610
Leave that here.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.740
By "that" do you mean this bouquet?

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:46.620
Yeah.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.660
Holding onto that just makes it
more likely for you to fall over.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.370
But this belongs to you.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.620
Look, it's...!

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.630
Fine, I get it.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:01.170
The bouquet belongs to me. Hand it over.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.010
Of course.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.930
Here is your bouquet, Mr. Customer.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.180
<i>My bouquet, huh?</i>

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.020
Thank you for accepting this.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.480
Yeah, yeah. I am a <i>garbage</i> collector, after all...

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.790
A liquor store...

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.290
Mr. Customer, may I ask you something?

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.550
Was this the result of a vehicle collision,
gas explosion, or other accident?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.680
Could be from combat, or a scavenger like me.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.260
An accident of sorts, I guess.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.850
If that is the case,
we must immediately call for rescue.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.940
It's already been dealt with.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.270
See, nobody's here anymore, right?

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.570
Yes. I understand the situation.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.740
They really blew this place up good. Wait here.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.530
Yes, understood.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.170
<i>Finally found a liquor store
and not a single damn thing's left.</i>

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.420
At least leave half of it standing...

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:27.180
Is that...?!

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:45.700
You'd be surprised at how
little it takes to kill a man.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.490
And here I had the impression
you'd survive stepping on a land mine.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.910
You got that right.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.920
A trap?

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.920
Usually when something kills you, that's it.
No second chances.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.680
<i>No wires or a weight-sensitive plate.</i>

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.720
<i>It could also be rigged up with...</i>

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.060
Here you are.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.490
After all that effort, this is all I get...

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:38.160
It appears that bottle you
have there is a scotch whiskey.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.920
A Twelve-year Sherry Barrel...

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.080
Price including tax is...

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.880
You know a lot of things. I'm impressed.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.050
Yes, thank you.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.510
Mr. Customer, is everything all right?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.650
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.070
<i>We're almost at the quarantine wall...</i>

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:16.540
<i>As long as we don't run into any complications,
we should be able to get through safely.</i>

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.540
Mr. Customer.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.710
There is a bump here, so please watch your step...

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.760
<i>For the fourteenth time...</i>

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.800
I told you to watch where you're going.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.680
I understand. My apologies.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.970
I'm surprised you're not in pieces by now.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.520
I am more durable than
my appearance may suggest.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.690
That's good to know.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:43.520
Yes.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:49.030
The streets really are empty.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.780
Yeah, it's just us.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:57.910
On rainy days like these,
we can't go outside, so it's very boring.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:02.540
However, spending time indoors could be fun too.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.170
Do you ever get bored?

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.670
Bored? What do you mean?

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:15.140
You've worked at the planetarium
for a long time, right?

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.260
Haven't you ever wanted to work a different job?

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:22.850
I am very fond of my job.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:30.070
Working with Mr. Manager, the staff,
and Miss Jena brings me much joy.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.030
I see.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:41.080
Mr. Customer, may I ask you something?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.330
What is it?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:47.500
Have you ever made a wish to God?

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:52.420
Perhaps, but nothing important.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:56.840
Come to think of it, I never asked
you what you would wish for.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.850
Yes, that is correct.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.810
What would you wish for?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.600
Please...

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.900
Please do not divide heaven in two.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:12.610
That is my prayer to the God of Robots.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.490
If people and robots were to be
separated at the Gates of Heaven,

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:20.200
then I would be truly worried.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.120
Even if I go to Heaven,

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.870
I still would like to be of service to all humans.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:29.000
I would like to be of assistance
to everyone, now and forever.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:31.800
Is that so...

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.050
Yes, it is!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:41.510
<i>If I leave her like this, her batteries will run dry.</i>

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:46.770
<i>If I'm to make her wish come true,
I would have to take her out of this city...</i>

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:51.400
<i>But can I force her to leave against her will?</i>

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:58.410
Mr. Customer, is your car still a long way away?

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.910
No, we're nearly there.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:05.370
Excellent. Shall we continue?

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.290
Yeah.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:13.300
<i>It must be because I had alcohol
for the first time in ages.</i>

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.170
<i>No...</i>

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.180
<i>I had already been drunk well past my limit</i>

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:25.060
<i>long before I encountered that bottle of whiskey.</i>

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.810
Even if it talks to you,

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.650
don't respond to it.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.530
Mr. Customer?

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.400
It's nothing. Let's go.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.320
<i>What am I to do with her?</i>

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:02.050
Mr. Customer, these streets are considerably
different from how they are on my database.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.100
Have the streets been redeveloped recently?

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.970
It's just as you see.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:10.100
Is that a construction machine of sorts over there?

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.060
It's a Fiddler Crab Autonomous Fire-support Mech.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.650
Can you elaborate?

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.610
Something not unlike yourself.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.190
<i>But there, of all places?</i>

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.490
<i>Right in front of the quarantine wall?</i>

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.950
<i>Can I make it?</i>

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.040
Mr. Customer?

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.370
I'm going hunting.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.750
Hunting?

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.080
Stay here until I come back.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:37.170
I'm leaving this city soon.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:40.840
What will you do after I leave you?

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:46.180
I will be able to walk myself back to
my workplace, so please do not worry.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:47.720
There's no one left in this city.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.890
Even if you were to return,
you'll never again have any customers,

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:52.980
and you'll never be able to show
the planetarium to anyone.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:55.860
Also, the power supply to this city is on its last legs.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.690
The projector will never operate again.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.570
You've seen all of this with your own two eyes!

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:06.950
Yes, but according to my base
and accumulated databases,

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:10.080
I believe that customers will surely come again.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.790
As for the power outage, both Miss Jena and I

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.460
are willing to wait as long as it takes
for the power to come back online.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.630
Look!

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:22.090
Listen <i>very</i> closely to what
I'm about to say, and listen well.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.090
Yes, understood.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:29.390
You saw the state of this city on your way here,
and I need you to make your choice based on that.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:32.980
This city no longer needs you <i>or the planetarium!</i>

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:38.770
If you want to continue working for humans,
you have to come with me.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:43.570
I don't know if that will make you happy.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:47.240
But I...

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:55.670
I believe that I wish to continue
serving all humans as well.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.960
That is what makes me happy.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:04.680
However, I believe that I have insufficient
data based on what you have told me

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.260
to decisively select a course of action.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.220
You have no means of gaining any more data.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.930
Don't you understand?

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.480
You have until I come back to think it over.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.490
Yes, understood.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.240
Oh, right. Hold on to this.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.740
Of course. I will handle it with care.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:33.750
Again, no matter what happens, don't move.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:37.000
Don't say a word until I come back.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.080
Understood.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.050
I have registered this as a critical directive.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.090
I will eagerly await your return.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:07.320
<i>A recharge station would be expensive,
but not impossible to obtain.</i>

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:12.280
<i>I could probably build her a small projector.</i>

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.540
<i>We could carry that around,
travel from colony to colony,</i>

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.370
<i>and show people the starry sky
together with her commentary.</i>

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:23.090
<i>That could be our new line of work.</i>

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.840
I must be losing it.

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:49.320
Sorry buddy, but I've got a partner again.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.040
It misfired?!
